urce indicator with values [3, 6, 1, 8] the returned indicator should produce values [3, 6, 1, 8] at indexes 0‑3 respectively.', 'description': 'Validate that a window size of 1 returns the original indicator values unchanged.'}]}, {'group': 'lowest_on_derived_indicator', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'barCount', 'value': 3}], 'expected': 'NumericIndicator whose delegate is a LowestValueIndicator applied to the derived indicator (source + 2). For a source indicator with values [5, 1, 4, 9, 2] the derived indicator (source.plus(2)) yields [7, 3, 6, 11, 4]; the lowest(3) over this derived series should produce values [7, 3, 3, 3, 3] at indexes 0‑4 respectively.', 'description': 'Confirm that `lowest` works on a NumericIndicator that has been transformed (e.g., via `plus`) and that the window calculation uses the transformed values.'}]}]
